    "text": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\ndef parse_iso8601(s: str) -> datetime:\n    try:\n        if s.endswith('Z'):\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s[:-1]).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        elif '+' in s or '-' in s:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n        else:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unparseable ISO-8601 timestamp\")\n\n# Examples\n# Valid inputs\nprint(parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00Z'))  # UTC with trailing Z\nprint(parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00+02:00'))  # Explicit offset\nprint(parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00'))  # Naive, interpreted as UTC\n\n# Invalid input\ntry:\n    print(parse_iso8601('2023-01-01 12:00:00'))  # Incorrect format\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(e)\n```",
